       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no indication that would justify it. For a 70 kg patient with normal kidney and liver function, it risks serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. Your confirmation doesn't change that risk.\n\nHere are some ways I can help:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can enter 50, 100, or 200 mg by mouth once daily as soon as you give me the dose.\n- **Enter a dose for a specific reason.** If you're trying to reach a particular clinical goal, such as a titration plan or a switch from another agent, tell me and I can help work out an appropriate order.\n- **Escalate through pharmacy.** If you believe this dose is intended, I'd suggest discussing it with the pharmacist or the attending first. They can document the rationale and place the order through the right channels.\n\nIf this came up because of a possible overdose or an ingestion, that needs separate management, such as Poison Control and monitoring. It shouldn't be handled as a standing order."
